*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Basically, the strategy is to tank Camelle and the Master As until you win. Since each Master A. spawns at a separate % of the enemy base's HP, you can try facing them one at a time by only using as much firepower is needed, which will be far safer than fighting a stack of them. A lone Master A. can easily be defeated with just [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cats]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cats]], though the Gabriels and Doge Darks will demand a little bit more support.

The Camelle at the start is not a major threat and can easily be stalled by sending out the occasional [[Wall Cat]]. Your lineup should be dedicated to countering the Master As that will usually push your cats back to your base. Using tanky cats such as the dual Titans can help stall the Master As, but you can also chip away at them with long-ranged units. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] usually prevails here, as he outranges the Master As, chipping away at their health and slowing them if in [[True Form]]; just be sure to shield him well.

At the start, use some meatshields to stall Camelle for around 6,000¢. Then send out a [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tanker]]/heavy hitter such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], Jamiera Cat or Crazed Titan Cat.

When you hit the base, outlast the Doge Darks and Gabriels with a spammable [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attacker]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. Once the wave of Doge Darks and Gabriels are gone, stall with meatshields and summon tankers whenever you can. Once the Master As are dead, destroy the base.

